# Imported-avatar framing and scale recovery

Status: DONE
Milestone: Correct same-source GLB/built-in size mismatch
Dependencies: 13_BLENDER_MODEL_RUNTIME.todo, 21_RECORDED_VIDEO_TEST_VIEW.todo

## Purpose
Remove the imported model's first-frame scale latch and prevent inferred depth from
inflating screen size. Preserve authored proportions, visibility rules and the original files.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect the supplied model and reproduce the mismatch using the supplied recording.
- [x] Verify that export dimensions are reasonable and locate the application-side scale latch.
- [x] Replace 3D/rest-length ratios with robust visible/projected rig-span ratios.
- [x] Update one smoothed uniform scale per detection rather than freezing the first estimate.
- [x] Reset scale history on source-size/timing changes, manual reset or loss of reliable evidence.
- [x] Add focused regressions for startup scale, depth noise, units, duplicate draws and bone lengths.
- [x] Finish complete-recording comparison and native checks.
- [x] Finish documentation, handbook, packaging and evidence readback.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] A recording starting with a partial/close-up pose recovers later framing without a reset.
- [x] Model scale at later full-body frames is comparable whether playback began there or earlier.
- [x] Display windows/mirroring do not update the scale twice for one observation.
- [x] Model-relative bone lengths, shape data and image-based visibility are preserved.
- [x] Inferred depth cannot inflate the measured screen-space span.
- [x] Supplied GLB/profile/video remain unchanged, with no raw/landmark exports or live camera.

## Completion evidence
- Reproduction latched scale1.460235 at2.128s with14eligible joints/partial body.
- Later old full-body estimates were2-4times smaller, but the saved value never changed.
- The old estimator also included inferred depth in display-size ratios. Projected estimates
  around15-19s are approximately0.29-0.31rather than0.39-0.65from the old formula.
-59focused regression cases passed again after restart;9model and10motion native groups passed.
- Complete2209-frame comparison passed. At18s, ongoing/fresh-start scale0.305634/0.303491;
  sampled full-body fits differ by at most3.8%. Full-body median size is22.6%of the old locked scale.
- Post-restart runtime check passed:28seconds,201inferred frames, fresh state and clean child exit.
  High frame skipping/render cost remains unqualified; this does not establish performance gains.
- Two pre-restart runtime checks failed to acquire frames. One measured89smodel loading;
  the slowdown's cause is not established, and both failed receipts are retained.
- Private baseline, comparisons and original-source archive: .local\scale-fix.
- Supplied model/profile/video are read-only; no Blender-side re-export or rescale is needed.
- Sanitized receipt:docs\evidence\imported-scale-validation.json. The earlier implementation
  receipt is preserved as before-scale-fix-validation.json.
- The82-page/175-citation handbook was rebuilt and its changed pages inspected. The wheel
